  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSac County, Iowa - County Government and Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Search\n \n \n \n\n \n\n About \n \n\n Boards & Commissions\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n Elected Officials\n School Districts\n Township Information\n \n \n \n\n Departments \n \n\n Ambulance Service\n Assessor\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Conservation\n County Attorney\n E-911\n Emergency Management\n General Assistance\n Human Resources\n Medical Examiner\n Planning and Zoning\n Public Health\n Recorder\n Roadside Program\n Secondary Roads\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n \n \n \n\n Resources \n \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n Careers\n Courts\n FAQ\n Landfill\n News\n Notifications\n \n \n \n\n Contact\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Search Sac County, Iowa\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n Alert Iowa \n \n \n\n \n \n Beacon \n \n \n\n \n \n Driver's License \n \n \n\n \n \n Meetings \n \n \n\n \n \n Property Tax \n \n \n\n \n \n Road Closures \n \n \n\n\n\n Explore all the County Offers\n \nWelcome to Sac County\n View Departments + Services\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Stay Up to Date with Sac County\n \nNews + Announcements\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Absentee Ballot Request Form\n \nPosted October 15\n \n \n\n Read Article \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n Notice of Bond Election\n \nPosted October 15\n \n \n\n Read Article \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n Notice of Election\n \nPosted October 15\n \n \n\n Read Article \n\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Sac County Calendar\n \nMeetings + Events\n \n \n\n View Full Calendar \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n19\n \nOctober\n \n Lake View Library Program\n 4:00 pm\n Lake View Public Library\n202 Main St, Lake View, IA 51450 · Lake View, IA \n\n \nLake View Library Program\n Lake View Public Library\n 202 Main St, Lake View, IA 51450\n Lake View, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 19, 2026 \n 4:00 pm · 5:00pm \n Cost: Free (All Ages) \n\nThis a monthly program at the Lake View Public Library for after school kids and the general public. Topic will change monthly. \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Dakota Popp \n(712) 662-4530 \n[email protected] \n \nPosted by: Conservation \n \n \n\n \n\n \n20\n \nOctober\n \n Board of Supervisors Meeting\n 10:00 am\n Sac County Courthouse\n100 NW State St · Sac City, IA \n\n \nBoard of Supervisors Meeting\n Sac County Courthouse\n 100 NW State St\n Sac City, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 20, 2026 \n 10:00 am \nPosted by: Board of Supervisors \n \n \n\n \n\n \n20\n \nOctober\n \n Sac County Quarterly 911 Service Board Meeting\n 7:00 pm\n Sac County Law Enforcement Center Conference Room\n100 NW State St., Suite 7 · Sac City, IA \n\n \nSac County Quarterly 911 Service Board Meeting\n Sac County Law Enforcement Center Conference Room\n 100 NW State St., Suite 7\n Sac City, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 20, 2026 \n 7:00 pm \n\nQuarterly 911 Service Board Meeting\n \n  \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Nichole Neumann \n(712) 662-7127 \n[email protected] \nWebsite\n \nPosted by: E-911 \n \n \n\n \n\n \n24\n \nOctober\n \n Sac County Pheasants Forever Youth Hunt\n 7:00 am\n Kiowa Marsh\n2397 230th st · Early, IA \n\n \nSac County Pheasants Forever Youth Hunt\n Kiowa Marsh\n 2397 230th st\n Early, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 24, 2026 \n 7:00 am · 1:00pm \n Cost: Free (11+) \n\nSac County Chapter of Pheasants Forever is putting on a Pheasant Youth Hunt for youth, ages 11-15, with a completed hunter safety education. This event will begin at the Iowa Department of Natural Resource building located outside of Early, Iowa. (2392 230th St, Early, IA) From there, we will go to public hunting accesses and pheasant hunt from 8-10AM. After the hunt we will come back and shoot clay pigeons. A light breakfast will be served starting at 7AM and we will finish the day with a pizza party. There will be give aways for all youth who attend. One lucky winner will even go home with a new shotgun! \n \n\nYouth must bring their own guns. Ammunition will be provided. Please dress appropriately for the hunt. A waiver of liability must be signed prior to attending. A parent/guardian is strongly encouraged to attend.\n \nThis event is pre-register only by calling or texting Paige Struchen at 712-292-0915, or private messaging the Sac County Chapter of Pheasants Forever Facebook page. Must register by October 15, 2025. Event is limited to the first 15 youth. \n \n\nInformation needed at the time of registering: child’s name, parent/guardian name if attending, caliber of gun they will be bringing, a copy of their hunter safety certificate, and signed waiver of liability form. \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Paige Struchen \n(712) 292-0915 \n \nPosted by: Conservation \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \nGet Outdoors\n \nSac County Parks\n \n\n \nFrom camping and hiking to canoeing and fishing, discover the many outdoor adventures awaiting. \n \n \nView Parks \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nAbout Our County \n \n\nEstablished in 1846, Sac County is a collection of 9 communities and home to nearly 9,000 residents. The county is named for the Sauk people, a local Native American tribe. Sac County is administered by a three-member Board of Supervisors who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nAddress\n 100 N W State Street\n \nSac City, IA 50583\n\n Contact Us\n \n \n\n \nCourthouse Hours\n M-F 8:00 am to 4:30 pm\n\n Closed Holidays\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Sac County | Title VI\n \npowered by \n \n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeteran's Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas (December 25, 2026)\n \nNew Years Day (January 1, 2027)\n \n\n"
